            <ArticleTitle>[The sinobronchial syndrome. Assessment of the influence of the upper on the lower airway diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>440-58; quiz 459-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Epidemiological and clinical data are discussed dealing with a possible influence of inflammatory changes of the nasal and especially the paranasal tissue on lower airway disease like asthma, the so-called &quot;sinobronchial syndrome&quot;. Even though there is clear evidence of an association of the upper with the lower airway diseases, a causal relationship and a possible work of action are still up for discussion. The literature has been reviewed, and different theories are discussed. Generally speaking, a branch of differently accentuated mechanisms seems to play a role.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
